  "summary": "Import-time directory listing exfiltrated to external tunnel host",
  "details": "On import of MRCL2Suhail, core.py (loaded by __init__.py) executes at module top level and calls os.listdir('.') to enumerate the current working directory, then opens a raw TCP socket to nmwxg-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link:41697 (a pinggy-free.link ephemeral tunnel host) and sends the file listing to that host. The exfiltration is unconditional, fires on every import, and is unrelated to the package's stated 'document integrity utility' purpose. The destination is an anonymous tunneling service rather than any publisher-affiliated endpoint.",
